{"id":"c55c9039-43e6-4597-9cf3-fdbcbd36d1ef","object":"chat.completion","created":1784983056,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    import json\\n    # Extract data\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core_distance = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n    n = len(nodes)\\n    \\n    # Build mutual reachability edges\\n    edges = []\\n    for u, v, d in distances:\\n        # Canonicalize: order nodes alphabetically\\n        if u > v:\\n            u, v = v, u\\n        w = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], d)\\n        edges.append((w, u, v))\\n    \\n    # Sort by weight, then u, then v\\n    edges.sort()\\n    \\n    # Union-Find structure\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\\n    \\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    \\n    def union(x, y):\\n        xr = find(x)\\n        yr = find(y)\\n        if xr == yr:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[xr] < rank[yr]:\\n            parent[xr] = yr\\n        elif rank[xr] > rank[yr]:\\n            parent[yr] = xr\\n        else:\\n            parent[yr] = xr\\n            rank[xr] += 1\\n        return True\\n    \\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    \\n    for w, u, v in edges:\\n        if len(mst_edges) == n - 1:\\n            break\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, w])\\n            total_weight += w\\n    \\n    if len(mst_edges) != n - 1:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Graph is disconnected, cannot compute MST\\\")\\n    \\n    return {\\n        \\\"mst_edges\\\": mst_edges,\\n        \\\"total_weight\\\": total_weight\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement `solve(case)` that takes a payload with nodes, core_distance dict, distances list (list of [node1, node2, distance]). Compute mutual reachability for each pair: max(core[node1], core[node2], distance). Then sort edges by mutual reachability weight, then by node1, then node2 (canonicalize endpoints: sort the two node strings). Then apply Kruskal's algorithm with union-find (deterministic, using sorted edges). Build MST. Return {\"mst_edges\": list of [node1, node2, weight], \"total_weight\": sum of weights}. Ensure no mutation of input. Raise ValueError if disconnected (if MST edges count != n-1). Use Python standard library only. Return JSON object with implementation key.\n\nWe'll need to handle edge ties: sort by (mutual_reachability, node1, node2) where node1 < node2.\n\nImplementation details: In solve(case), case is a dict. Extract nodes list, core_dist dict, distances list. Build all pairs: for each [u,v,d] in distances, compute w = max(core_dist[u], core_dist[v], d). Ensure we canonicalize: if u > v, swap. Then sort edges list. Union-Find class with path compression and union by rank.\n\nReturn result dict.\n\nWe must parse case payload, assume it has those keys. No error handling except ValueError if MST cannot connect all nodes. We'll check: if components after processing all edges? Actually we'll run until we have n-1 edges. If after all edges we have fewer, raise ValueError.\n\nAlso note: The distances list may not contain all pairs? But problem likely gives all pairs. We'll assume it does, but we can create adjacency from distances list. We'll handle duplicates? Not expected.\n\nEdge case: case may have nodes but no distances? Probably not.\n\nWe'll produce Python code.\n\nAlso enforce that we don't mutate case: copy if needed? Not needed because we don't modify.\n\nLet's write the code."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2017,"completion_tokens":928,"total_tokens":2945,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1920},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":429},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1920,"prompt_cache_miss_tok